    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d599">

                <pb facs="0677" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg665"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.9131/108: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-02-03T21:00:00+03:25">February 3, 1940—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 5—4:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>26. Personal for Murray.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d599-f1"/> My 25 of today.
                    Whatever the ultimate reaction of our competent authorities might be to the
                    scheme outlined may I suggest that a courteous reply be sent at once indicating
                    that it would be given serious consideration? Such a reply, coming at a
                    psychological moment when we are trying to break a deadlock in connection with
                    the evaluation of school properties,<anchor n="63" xml:id="d599-f2"/> might
                    help.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d599-f1" n="62" xml:id="d599-f1-content">
                <p>Wallace Murray, Chief of the Division of Near Eastern Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d599-f2" n="63" xml:id="d599-f2-content">
                <p>Missionary school properties expropriated by the Iranian Government. For
                    correspondence, see <ref target="#pg693">pp. 693</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
